Detective Ellis Brooks is a weathered looking middle-aged human male. He has graying hair that he hides under a fedora, and a wearied look that can only be developed after years on the police force. He wears an open brown peacoat with a disheveled white button-down underneath, and carries a pistol in a holster on his chest over the shirt. He has a moderately sized raiment of the [[Iridescent Host|Host]].

Brooks is a no-nonsense detective, but he's seen everything and has learned to trust his gut rather than dismiss the strange outright. He wishes he could get back out into tracking down leads instead of coordinating behind a desk, but he knows he's too good at what he does now to be able to justify anything else.

He has worn the badge for a hundred years. On [[Org/The Scale/People/Dame Quay|Dame Quay]]'s word he took the Party on as paid consultants to the convox, but he would not open an investigation into [[Org/Amber Call/People/Benjamin Grayson|Grayson]], who sits on the council that rules [[Geography/Calaria/index|Calaria]], saying it would put his neck on the line and theirs with it.

Brooks has since resigned from the [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Magical Crimes/index|Magical Crimes Convox]] and vanished. His rented flat in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Prism Heights/index|Prism Heights]] was found with blood sprayed beside the bed, cut by three claw grooves too big for the undead the Party fought there, and a trail leading to the window. There was not blood enough to say he died there.
